  "text": "Haiku 4.5 subagent validation - SUCCESSFUL:\n\n**Researcher subagent:**\n- Time: ~2 minutes\n- Context savings: 56k → 500 tokens (99% reduction)\n- Quality: Excellent research with proper citations\n- Use case: Read massive docs, output concise summaries\n\n**Test-generation subagent:**\n- Time: 94 seconds\n- Output: 1153 lines of production code\n- Tests: 20 cases, 81 assertions, all passing\n- Context savings: ~35k → 500 tokens (98.5% reduction)\n- Quality: A+ production-ready tests\n- Use case: Generate comprehensive tests for existing code\n\nBoth subagents are proving the multi-agent orchestration approach works:\n1. Primary agent (Sonnet 4.5) maintains architectural context\n2. Subagents (Haiku 4.5) handle isolated, well-defined tasks\n3. Results returned as small summaries\n4. Massive context savings enable longer sessions\n\nThis is exactly what the research predicted: \"Delegate 30-40% of work to Haiku saves 60-70% on tokens while maintaining quality.\"\n\nNext steps to consider:\n- Document these subagent patterns for future use\n- Consider additional subagents (documentation generation, refactoring)\n- Track context savings over time to validate ROI",
